WEBVTT

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.020
Shiki?

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.770
S-Sorry I woke you.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.230
Wearing your school uniform on a Sunday?

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.880
Are you going to school?

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.200
Yeah. My club has a quiz meet today.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.080
Club? A meet?!

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.070
Y-Yeah.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.590
I had no idea!

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.540
What about lunch? 
I'll pack you one right away!

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:26.600
<i>My memories of my dad reading 
books to me when I was little</i>

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.390
<i>seem so far away in my memory now.</i>

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.790
<i>For me, reading was a way for me
 to have fun in my own little world.</i>

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.510
I'm borrowing this book today.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.810
<i>I learned a lot of things in 
my world spun from letters.</i>

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:45.800
<i>It's my own secret world, 
which I've kept warm all this time.</i>

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.850
<i>And now, it's starting to connect me 
with the world everyone else inhabits...</i>

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.230
<i>The quiz bowl world.</i>

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:54.960
<i>Okay!</i>

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.210
<b>Question 8: "\Greetings/ Asagaoka Regular Meet!"</b>

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:31.310
Thank you all for participating in 
today's regular meet here at Asagaoka.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.960
Once you've signed in, 
please sit wherever you like.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.880
We're having a quiz meet 
in a place like this?

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.290
Looks fun!

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.110
Keep it down, Jinko.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:45.220
The rule is that spectators can't 
interfere with participants.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.150
Yukicchi! It's been half 
a month since I saw you!

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.480
There, there. We can hang 
out again starting from today.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.360
What's that about?

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.860
A gag order.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:58.820
We were told not to associate with 
students from other schools until the meet.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.030
The host school is in charge of 
managing the questions and rules.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.910
<b>Present</b>

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.360
To avoid unnecessary misunderstandings,

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:03.910
<b>Inoue Daisuke 
Koshiyama Shiki 
Sasajima Gakuto 
Fukami Mari</b>

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.360
they must take care when 
 associating with participating schools.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.540
Huh?

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.160
They're doing it by the book, huh?

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.380
So Ashiya-kun, your tests 
are in two days, aren't they?

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.500
Niina...

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.220
There's no way I could miss this meet when 
kids from my school are participating.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.590
Mikuriya, what are you doing?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:21.880
What are you—

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.350
<i>Question: Kyoto's Golden Pavilion 
and Silver Pavilion are—</i>

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:24.980
Give that back!

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.440
He's listening to questions!

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.560
Seriously?!

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.310
<i>Mikuriya-kun...</i>

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.530
<i>So you came, Koshiyama.</i>

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:35.770
<i>I hope you've been brushing up.</i>

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.930
<i>A quiz competition with Mikuriya-kun...</i>

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:39.420
<i>I can't wait!</i>

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.070
It's Kaijou Academy.

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:47.430
The veteran quiz team and 
champions of the east.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.910
So Kaijou's club president 
this year is Ohkura, huh?

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.560
He ranked first on the national 
mock exams in literature.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.880
<b>Kaijou High School 2nd Year 
Ohkura Kunimitsu</b>

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.880
No one can match him on the paper quiz.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:59.090
<i>Kaijou Academy's quiz team... 
That's where my brother used to play!</i>

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.990
Kaijou, eh? They look tough again this year.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:06.430
They all look really impressive.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.810
Kaijou isn't the only tough school here.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:12.020
Sekigawata, whose club 
president is Niina-san...

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.770
Miyaura, whose president is Ashiya-san...

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.360
And then there's Yokohama 
Kannami University High School...

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:18.870
and Chiba's Leoneil.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.860
They're all equally prestigious schools.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.160
Whoa! Whazzat?

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:33.210
Welcome to the Asagaoka Regular Meet.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:38.910
As the Bible teaches, "Those who 
think they know something

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:43.300
do not yet know as they ought to know."

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:49.130
It also says, "As iron sharpens iron, 
so one person sharpens another."

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.080
Young ones, apply yourselves to the fullest!

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:54.770
May God bless you and keep you.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:56.880
Amen.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.650
<i>Nailed it.</i>

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:08.240
Today's events will proceed in the order 
outlined in the programs you received at sign-in.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.740
<i>So this is today's program...</i>

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.370
We are now distributing paper quizzes.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.080
<b>In the Beginning, There Was The Word</b>

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.580
Round 1 will now begin.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.780
You have ten minutes.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.030
<i>The paper quiz is fifty questions,</i>

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:25.660
<i>including one that calls for approximation.</i>

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.880
<i>Religious stuff right off the bat...</i>

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.390
<i>Looks like this is going to 
follow us around all day.</i>

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:36.940
You have one minute left.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.900
Thirty seconds.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.650
Stop.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.520
We will now take a break.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:48.080
The answers will be announced at 12:00, 
and rankings will be announced at 12:10.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.910
Koshiyama, let's go see what an 
all-girls school looks like!

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.700
Sorry, I'll pass.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:48.780
Oh, fine...

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.830
Inoue-kun, let's go get some drinks.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.290
Sure!

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.870
Man, what a drag.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.630
Don't stand there and drink it! Move!

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.400
Sorry.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.520
Huh? Where have I...

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.160
Bullseye.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:19.940
Sasajima.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:22.190
Ohkura.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.030
<i>Wh-What does Kaijou's club president 
have to say to Sasajima-senpai?!</i>

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.910
You finally showed up, Sasajima?!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.160
Uh, well, looks that way, yeah...

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.210
I've waited for you this whole time!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:39.100
I heard rumors that you started 
a quiz team at Buzou,

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.420
and I thought to myself, "Now's the time!"

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:43.610
Okay, I get it. Now, get off 
me. You're in my face.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.510
Quickly, accurately, and efficiently!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:48.230
Yes!

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:49.880
I've finished scoring the first one!

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.890
Um, President...

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.140
This person got most of the answers right,

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:58.750
but somehow, all the answers from 
Question 4 onward are a space off.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.740
Huh? Who did that?

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:01.730
Does that mean...

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.730
Naturally. Mark them all as incorrect.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:05.860
What a waste...

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.320
<i>The high-ranking players with the 
real skills are a cut above the others.</i>

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:13.470
<i>They're even getting the toughest 
questions we could throw at them.</i>

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.290
<i>I look forward to the remaining rounds.</i>

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.790
<b>Question 2</b>

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.790
<b>June Bride</b>

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.790
The answer to Question 2 was "June bride."

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:22.150
You haven't been to a meet 
since last summer, have you?

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:23.170
Guess not.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.210
Does this mean you're back 
on the quiz bowl scene?

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.760
I don't believe I ever left.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:33.720
But Senpai mourned the loss of 
his most promising rookie, his ace.

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:39.480
Losing one or two members doesn't 
diminish Kaijou's strength one bit.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:43.480
Besides, no matter where I go, 
I can still do quiz bowl.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.950
They're announcing the answers.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:49.230
Huh? We don't get our answer sheets back?

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:52.180
I guess not. Just like with entrance exams,

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.700
people who want to know how they 
did can grade their own work.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.820
I guess this was a step too far, after all.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.160
Current affairs, anime, 
show business, fashion...

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:02.170
I can't keep up with all 
this new information.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.220
Probably 'cause you're always 
readin' stuffy old books.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.630
I tend to lean more toward the 
classics, because I like them best.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:14.200
My mom always tells me I got 
my taste in books from my dad.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.720
He died, though.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:22.330
Even now, I still binge-read 
his books all the time.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:25.810
And they're all masterpieces 
from way back when.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:31.210
But I think I might need to start 
reading different kinds of books.

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:33.780
You can take it slow, can't you?

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.390
It's awesome that your knowledge 
came from reading your dad's books.

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:39.240
That's a fine weapon to have.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:43.240
Mastering your best subject, or 
conquering categories you don't excel in...

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.600
All of you have only just begun 
on your quiz bowl journey.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.710
There's no need to rush.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:51.800
Next, the announcement you've all been 
waiting for: your rankings on the paper quiz.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.000
The top ten will advance to Round 3,

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.260
and everyone else will 
participate in Round 2.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.390
Taking first place...

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:03.140
<b>st</b>

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:03.140
<b>points</b>

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:03.120
With 47 points,

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:06.270
<b>Buzou High School, 2nd Year</b>

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:06.270
<b>Sasajima Gakuto</b>

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:06.270
Sasajima Gakuto-kun, second-year, 
from Buzou High School.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.690
Seriously?!

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.810
<i>He's on Buzou's rookie team now,</i>

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:16.860
<i>but he's the real deal. 
It's clear he came from Kaijou.</i>

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:18.530
Congratulations.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.040
Buzou High School is participating 
for the first time this year.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.240
How do you feel about today?

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:27.300
I hope the younger members of my club 
will gain a lot from today's meet.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:29.710
And for you, personally?

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:31.880
I intend to enjoy myself.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.630
<i>Sasajima-senpai's so cool!</i>

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:37.680
Next, in second place...

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:39.600
<b>nd</b>

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.450
With the same score as the top finisher...

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.560
<b>Kaijou High School 2nd Year</b>

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.560
<b>Ohkura Kunimitsu</b>

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:42.560
Ohkura Kunimitsu-kun, second-year, 
from Kaijou High School.

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:44.760
Ah, so close.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:48.150
The same score means you only missed 
out on first by the approximation question.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
Schoolyard

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
East
Building

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
Audito-
rium

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
Hall A

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
Court-
yard

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
<b>Chapel</b>

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
West 
Building

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
Front
 Yard

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
School 
Building

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.020
Hall B

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:51.800
It asked for an approximation of the 
total area of the Asagaoka campus.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.800
When the exact number is unknown,

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:58.010
you make a rough, theoretical 
estimate based on a few assumptions.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.110
The Fermi estimate.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:01.830
That's probably how Sasajima calculated it.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:06.080
I looked it up on Asagaoka's 
homepage beforehand.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.330
I knew it might turn up on the quiz.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:11.540
His intuition is often right.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:18.510
<b>Miyaura High School 3rd Year</b>

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:18.510
<b>Ashiya Yousuke</b>

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.040
Next, in third place with 39 points,

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:18.510
Ashiya Yousuke-kun, third-year, 
from Miyaura High School.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.220
All right!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.310
In fourth place with 38 points,

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:25.250
Konoe Haruomi-kun, second-year, 
from Kaijou High School.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:25.850
<b>Kaijou High School 2nd Year 
Konoe Haruomi</b>

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:25.850
Yes!

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.050
In fifth place with 38 points,

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:31.440
Tozuka Koutarou-kun, third-year, 
from Leoneil High School.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:31.440
<b>Leoneil High School 3rd Year
Tozuka Koutarou</b>

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.770
In sixth place with 37 points,

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.030
Shibuya Hiroki-kun, third-year, 
from Kannami University High School.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.030
<b>Kannami University 
High School 3rd Year 
Shibuya Hiroki</b>

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:38.990
In seventh place with 36 points,

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:42.240
Shibata Masaru-kun, second-year, 
from Kaijou High School.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.240
<b>Kaijou High School 2nd Year 
Shibata Masaru</b>

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.650
In eighth place with 35 points,

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:47.430
Hanabusa Minoru-kun, third-year, 
from Kannami University High School.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:48.330
<b>Kannami University 
High School Third-Year 
Hanabusa Minoru</b>

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:48.330
Yay!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.410
In ninth place with 35 points,

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:53.610
Hosokawa Atsuyoshi-kun, first-year, 
from Kaijou High School.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:54.040
<b>Kaijou High School 1st Year 
Hosokawa Atsuyoshi</b>

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:56.870
And last but not least, 
in tenth place, with 33 points...

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.930
<b>Miyaura High School 1st Year</b>

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.930
<b>Mikuriya Chisato</b>

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:01.460
Mikuriya Chisato-kun, first-year, 
from Miyaura High School.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.150
Look at Mikuriya's name!

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.310
<b>Lieutenant Colonel 
Chisato 
Pts: 325,875 
Tokyo Major 
Land Akihabara</b>

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.530
No way...

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:18.780
I scored my own quiz, and I 
should've made the top ten!

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:21.490
<i>Ah, he's the one whose 
answers were off by one space.</i>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:29.000
<b>Miyaura High School 1st Year</b>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:29.000
<b>Mikuriya Chisato</b>

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:25.610
These ten will advance to 
the third round as seeds.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:29.000
Everyone else will proceed to 
Round 2, the fastest finger round.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.040
<b>You'll be in it?! 
Can I come watch?!</b>

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>I-I'll be in it, 
but I don't think
 you can watch</b>

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:31.460
<b>I thought you
 were just 
obsessed with 
quiz bowl</b>

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:31.960
<b>So you really 
<i>can</i> do quiz 
bowl, Senpai...</b>

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:32.670
<b>What do you guys 
take me for?</b>

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.210
We will now continue on to Round 2.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.480
The two of us will be your commentators...

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:42.790
Asagaoka third-year, Sonohara Chiaki.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:45.010
First-year, Kouzuki Yuki.

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:48.550
If there's anything you don't 
understand, just ask me, Yuki-san.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:50.730
Y-Yes, O-Onee-sama!

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:54.220
Round 2: The "Thou shalt
love thy neighbor as thyself"

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:56.610
five right, two wrong fastest finger quiz!

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.570
<b>Round 2</b>

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.570
<b>"Thou Shalt Love Thy 
Neighbor As Thyself"</b>

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.570
<b>5 O 2 X   Fastest Finger Quiz</b>

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:59.570
I will now explain the rules.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:04.510
Participants in Round 2 will 
draw cards to form pairs.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.630
Each participant will have a buzzer,

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:08.780
but they will be scored as a pair.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.200
<b>Up to 25 Questions</b>

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:12.990
It will be a five right, two wrong fastest 
finger quiz with up to 25 questions.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.330
<b>Fastest Finger Quiz</b>

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:16.620
A correct answer earns a "Right" mark, and 
an incorrect answer earns a "Wrong" mark.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.590
<b>Marks Win!</b>

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.110
Five "Right" marks mean you win the round,

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:19.590
<b>Marks Disqualify</b>

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:19.840
and two "Wrong" marks mean disqualification.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:25.470
<b>Each Question Has Two Answers</b>

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:25.580
However, each question in this 
quiz will have two answers.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:29.380
The buzzer of the participant 
who buzzes in first will blink,

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:30.530
and their partner's will glow.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.540
The question will continue to be 
read until two people have buzzed in.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.480
<b>Quiz Quiz  /  Quiz  /</b>

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:38.730
<b>Up to Two Can Answer Each Question</b>

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:38.430
Up to two participants can earn the 
right to answer each question.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.160
If both members of 
a pairing answer correctly,

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.120
it counts as three "Right" marks,

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.610
but they must answer in the 
order that they buzzed.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.110
There will be no conferring.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:50.960
Pairs? Two correct answers per 
question? Two can buzz in?

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.410
You've really thought this out, Asagaoka!

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:54.420
Are these rules uncommon?

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.640
They're certainly unorthodox.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.560
Quiz questions and formats 
have infinite possibilities,

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:01.050
depending on what the creator comes up with.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.840
This should be a good competition.

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:07.590
A sun?

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:10.090
A sun? That's me.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:13.390
I'm Yagi, and I'm a first-year at 
Kannami University High School.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.730
I'm no good at quiz bowl yet, though.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.980
I'm Fukami, a first-year at Buzou.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:21.070
I'm not that confident, either. 
Let's just try our hardest, okay?

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:25.200
The first group of pairs in 
Round 2 has been determined.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:29.100
Only one pair from each 
group can win the round.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.200
This will test the love 
between each partner!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.450
<i>Time to make up for botching the paper quiz!</i>

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.840
<i>This is as great as I thought it'd be!</i>

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:53.060
Group A in this two-answers-
per-question quiz will now begin!

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:54.520
Question.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.930
The three largest religions 
in the world are Christ—

00:13:58.580 --> 00:13:59.310
Buddhism!

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:00.210
Islam!

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:01.150
Correct.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.400
<i>Numerated format...</i>

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:08.530
<b>Q: The three largest religions in the world are 
Christianity, what, and what?    A: Buddhism, Islam</b>

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:05.710
I get it!

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:08.530
Since there are two answers, the 
determining points are different!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.030
What do ya mean by that?

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:14.540
If you buzz in where you would if the question 
had only one answer, you'll be too late.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:19.500
<b>Group</b>

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:19.500
Yamada x Gotou

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:19.500
Fukami x Yagi

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:19.500
Niina x Takahashi

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:19.500
Ohki x Miyazaki

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:15.760
Question.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:20.770
Of all the prefectural capitals, the kanji 
meaning "capital" is used in which—

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:23.850
<i>All of their reactions 
slowed for an instant.</i>

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:25.070
<i>So even if the question's easy,</i>

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:28.430
<i>the answer doesn't come to mind easily 
when there are a lot of possible answers?</i>

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.000
Uh... Kyoto!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:34.220
No way! I was gonna say Kyoto!

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:35.930
Please give the other answer.

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:37.310
<i>It's not Tokyo...</i>

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.090
Utsunomiya... That's it! Utsunomiya!

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.480
<b>Q: Of all the prefectural capitals, the kanji meaning 
"capital" is used in which two names?  A: Kyoto, Utsunomiya</b>

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:44.890
<i>So you have to come up with both answers...</i>

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:46.740
<i>That makes it much harder 
if you're the second to guess.</i>

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.360
Fukami x Yagi

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.360
Niina x Takahashi

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:51.700
Sorry, Fukami-san. I can't even buzz in.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.510
It's okay. I can't, either.

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:54.830
But it's still early.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:15:00.580
<i>In questions with two answers, the harder 
answer tends to be left till last.</i>

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.500
<i>But that doesn't always mean the 
second one will be hard to guess.</i>

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:04.750
Question.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:08.440
Napoleon's invasion of Russia is 
the backdrop for Tolstoy's—

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.180
<i>Fukami-san buzzed in!</i>

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:12.010
Please give the first answer.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:12.930
War and—

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.140
<i>Crap! I added the "and"!</i>

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:20.050
<i>Sometimes the first answer gives 
a hint that leads to the second.</i>

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:21.100
War and...

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:22.820
Peace.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:23.790
Correct.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:25.900
<b>Q: Napoleon's invasion of Russia is the backdrop for 
Tolstoy's literary masterpiece titled "What" and "What"?  A: War, Peace</b>

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:26.310
Yes!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.660
<b>Group</b>

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.660
Yamada x Gotou

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.660
Fukami x Yagi

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.660
Niina x Takahashi

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.660
Ohki x Miyazaki

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.660
Takamura x Satou

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:29.430
The Niina x Takahashi pairing has three 
"Right" marks and one "Wrong" mark.

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:31.660
Each of the other pairs 
has one "Right" mark.

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:33.870
Yagi-san, let's buzz in on the next one.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:36.610
Huh? But I might get it wrong!

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:39.150
The questions haven't 
been that difficult so far.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:42.080
And in fastest finger, if you 
don't earn the right to answer,

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.790
you get nowhere.

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:45.890
Okay!

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:47.600
Question.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.920
The countries whose official 
names include "United States"—

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:52.930
That was impressive!

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.510
The Fukami x Yagi pair has the 
exclusive right to answer!

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:57.350
The first answer, please, Fukami-san.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:16:03.020
<i>Um... The first one that comes to mind 
is America, but the other one...</i>

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:05.190
The United Mexican States.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:08.420
Correct. The second answer, please.

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:09.950
America!

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.400
<b>Q: The countries whose official names include "United States" are 
what and what?  A: United States of America, United Mexican States</b>

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:10.890
Correct.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:13.360
We did it!

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:16.430
<i>She got the harder answer for me...</i>

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:18.580
<i>She's so reliable and nice!</i>

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.040
<b>Group</b>

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.040
Yamada x Gotou

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.040
Fukami x Yagi

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.040
Niina x Takahashi

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.040
Ohki x Miyazaki

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.040
Takamura x Satou

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:21.040
The Fukami x Mari pairing 
earn three "Right" marks.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.000
That gives them four in 
total. One more to win!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.160
All right!

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:25.460
They just need one more!

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:28.770
Only one pair from each 
group will win the round.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:30.090
What's going to happen?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:30.840
<i>I won't lose this!</i>

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.090
<i>I've got to push on through!</i>

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:33.550
Question.

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:35.560
Mesopotamian civilization was cultivated—

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:38.680
Yes!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:41.900
The Tigris River!

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:42.640
Correct!

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:45.710
The Fukami x Yagi pairing has won the round!

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:46.900
Congratulations!

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.540
Fukami-san made it to Round 3!

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:59.080
Yes. Her understanding of the rules and 
teamwork with her partner led her to victory.

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:02.290
Participants in the next group, 
please take to the stage.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.090
I guess I'm up now...

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:05.930
Have fun!

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:07.980
O-Okay!

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:11.760
<i>I just hope I get a strong partner...</i>

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.610
He's with Maruyama-kun from Miyaura!

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:17.140
It's nice to get someone we know.

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:20.120
Well, we did have a joint practice together.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:21.650
Let's do this thing.

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:23.540
What are your best categories?

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.380
Classics. Omnivores.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:26.850
Is that even a category?

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:28.810
We will now begin.

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:30.160
Question.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:33.340
Leading out from the human 
heart are two major arteries—

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:35.150
Kumada-kun from Kaijou buzzed in first.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:36.470
Aorta.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:39.510
Nakamura-kun from Kannami 
buzzed in second.

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:40.690
Pulmonary artery.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.580
<b>Q: Leading out from the human heart are two major
arteries known as what and what?  A: Aorta, pulmonary artery</b>

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.140
Damn, that was fast!

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.410
Hey, aren't you good at classics?!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.000
That sounded like a classic! 
You should've buzzed!

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:47.920
I did!

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:50.920
They're arguin'. Think they'll be okay?

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.630
Kumada x Hirosue

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.630
Maruyama x Inoue

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.630
Nakamura x Nakazawa

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:54.140
<i>This is hopeless.</i>

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:55.590
<i>I can't buzz in time.</i>

00:17:55.970 --> 00:18:00.180
You buzz in when you think you can get 
it, then use your thinking time wisely.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.200
We've gone over that a ton in practice.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:03.060
You can do it!

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:06.610
It's not that Inoue-kun and his 
partner don't know the answer.

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:08.270
They just need to buzz faster.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.150
Really?

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:12.670
The question is whether they can answer 
within five seconds after buzzing.

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:15.800
Making that judgment within a mere 0.01 seconds...

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:17.040
If you hesitate, you'll be beaten.

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:21.530
When you have to weigh up the risk 
of getting a wrong answer,

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:25.000
you might have no choice 
but to be a little reckless.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:28.050
Just don't let 'em beat ya 
in spirit, no matter what!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.520
Question.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:32.420
Kumada x Hirosue

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:32.420
Maruyama x Inoue

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:32.420
Nakamura x Nakazawa

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:32.420
Japan is home to two types of wildcats—

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:33.880
Oh, you're second!

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:37.840
Yeah, but... Sorry, I only 
know one of the answers.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:39.720
Iriomote cat.

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:42.540
Maruyama-kun, the second answer, please.

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:45.270
As if I know! Uraomote cat!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:49.480
<b>Q: Japan is home to two types of wildcats, the 
what and the what?  A: Iriomote cat, Tsushima cat</b>

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:49.480
The other answer was the Tsushima cat.

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:53.190
<i>The scary part about this format is 
when you lose the race to buzz in first</i>

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:55.900
<i>and end up unwillingly being 
the second to buzz in.</i>

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:03.870
<b>Group</b>

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:03.870
Tani x Suwa

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:03.870
Kumada x Hirosue

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:03.870
Maruyama x Inoue

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:03.870
Nakamura x Nakazawa

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:03.870
Inamori x Namiki

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:58.290
That's one "Wrong" mark for 
the Maruyama x Inoue pairing.

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.110
They can't get any more questions wrong.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:03.870
One pair has four "Right" marks. 
The next question could decide the round!

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:05.580
<i>Is this the end?</i>

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:08.290
<i>I wanted to answer at least one...</i>

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:09.540
Question.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:11.580
The "Three Views of Japan"—

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:13.320
He buzzed!

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:14.080
There?!

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:14.920
Too soon!

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:18.630
The Maruyama x Inoue pair has 
the exclusive right to answer!

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:21.340
<i>For the "Three Views of Japan," 
do they want the locations?</i>

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:23.560
<i>Judging from how the questions 
have been up to this point,</i>

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:25.850
<i>it's probably just the standard 
Three Views of Japan.</i>

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:30.560
<i>The crucial part is which two of the 
three answers they're looking for.</i>

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.840
<i>I buzzed in just because I 
heard a term I knew, but...</i>

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:38.780
<b>Three Views of Japan</b>

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:35.950
<i>The Three Views of Japan 
I learned in middle school</i>

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:38.780
<i>are Matsushima, Miyajima, 
and Amanohashidate.</i>

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:38.780
<b>Matsushima</b>

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.780
<b>Miyajima</b>

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:38.780
<b>Amanohashidate</b>

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:41.740
The first answer, please, Inoue-kun.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.520
<i>Well, I know two of those are the answers.</i>

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:47.700
<i>N-No problem! I just need to say one!</i>

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:53.000
<i>I have to bet it all on a 
two-out-of-three chance!</i>

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:55.960
Amanohashidate!

00:19:57.650 --> 00:19:59.420
Inoue-kun, that's incorrect.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:03.090
Unfortunately, the Maruyama x 
Inoue pairing has two "Wrong" marks,

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.410
and has been disqualified.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.300
Man, I lost.

00:20:08.300 --> 00:20:10.010
But I guess them's the breaks.

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:11.960
Inoue...

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.360
You tried really hard, though!

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:17.150
It takes guts to buzz in that early!

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.770
It blew up in my face, though.

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:21.760
If there had been one correct answer,

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:24.030
Amanohashidate might have 
been the right guess.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:32.210
<b>Matsushima 
Miyajima 
Amanohashidate</b>

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:41.460
<b>The Three Views of Japan</b>

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:29.830
In numerated format questions, 
one of the possible answers

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.130
is usually radically different,

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:35.300
while the other two have 
something in common.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:37.920
<b>Matsushima 
Miyajima 
Amanohashidate</b>

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:41.460
And when there's only one answer, 
the one that's different is usually correct.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:41.460
<b>Matsushima 
Miyajima 
Amanohashidate</b>

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:45.930
But when questions in the numerated 
format have two answers...

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:48.650
I get it! It works the opposite way,

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:49.140
<b>Matsushima 
Miyajima 
Amanohashidate</b>

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:50.560
<b>The Three Views of Japan</b>

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:50.560
so the two that are similar are the answers!

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.560
<b>Matsushima 
Miyajima 
Amanohashidate</b>

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:56.690
But there's no guarantee that the question's 
composition will follow any sort of rule.

00:20:57.350 --> 00:21:00.030
And that's why determining 
points are crucial.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:02.950
That's really interesting...

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:07.950
It's not just the people answering that 
have to think about the questions.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:15.160
Participants in the next 
group, please get ready.

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:17.130
Here I go.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.380
That kid...

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:24.780
Every time he learns something 
new, he calls it "interesting."

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:28.100
I just feel more and more 
like I can't keep up.

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:32.810
If ya ask me, I think you're pretty 
amazin' yourself, Taishou.

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:33.920
Huh?

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.210
Mari, you were sayin' the 
same thing, weren't ya?

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:38.230
About how it takes guts to buzz in.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:43.440
Competitions are a game of chance.
 Today's loss will lead to tomorrow's win!

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:44.770
Ya did just great!

00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:47.700
Jinko-san... Thank ya kindly!

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:50.700
What's with that Kansai dialect? 
Your pronunciation's all wrong.

00:21:50.920 --> 00:21:52.160
Huh?

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:57.290
<i>It's not just the people answering 
that think about the questions.</i>

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:01.060
<i>The people who write the 
questions think hard about them,</i>

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:04.480
<i>and a lot of detailed planning 
goes into coming up with them.</i>

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:08.210
<i>If I can read into that and understand it...</i>

00:22:09.900 --> 00:22:14.550
Well, it's time for the next 
group to start, Onee-sama.

00:22:14.550 --> 00:22:19.290
Which pairing will advance to Round 3?

00:22:30.520 --> 00:22:32.740
The regular meet at Asagaoka 
has finally begun!

00:22:33.230 --> 00:22:36.210
Now, take this mic and tell me 
how you feel about this meet!

00:22:36.640 --> 00:22:38.800
All right, I'll go first.

00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:42.090
I will have you all at my 
mercy with my quiz questions!

00:22:42.770 --> 00:22:45.050
I'll show you the pride of a public school!

00:22:45.450 --> 00:22:46.810
For the Buzou quiz circle...

00:22:46.810 --> 00:22:48.050
Victory!

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:52.010
The long-established Sekigawata 
will win for sure!

00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:56.020
I'm so glad you're back, Sasajima!

00:22:56.310 --> 00:22:59.680
Yes, yes! How wonderful it is to be young!
